ce confronted them  there  police have also been closing in on the  farmers campsites  using rows of barricades and barbed wire  the police is digging up  uh trenches and building fortifications  around the farmers protest sites  as though they are preparing for a war  but they've gone further than that  jammed internet access around protest  sites in new delhi  ordered twitter to block accounts of  farmers unions  and news outlets and charged  certain journalists with sedition over  their report  and then there's the media wars  especially after western celebrities  started commenting on the crackdown  and indian celebrities hit back  [Music]  hitting back gangnam tweeted saying that  greta  is a dumbo kid and a spoiled brat who  made a big blunder by revealing the  international plot to defame india  so this has snowballed into something  bigger than just farming they're talking  about people's right to dissent  police violence even the whole idea of  democracy in india  and some say party politics are making  it all worse  critics of prime minister narendra modi  think he's creating business  opportunities for his rich friends  then you've got the ruling party and  state media blaming the protests on  opposition groups  the banned terror outfit communist party  of india maoist  has infiltrated the farm protests they  point to these protesters waving a sikh  flag  as proof that separatists from the north  are involved too the poor farmer  feels that their land will be taken away  snatched by  these giant corporate but we have put a  safety net  the apprehension is primarily the  handiwork of the upa  members particularly the fiscal  opposition party i think the government  would like  nothing more than to see the protest  ending  but the farmers they will only move if  their  demands are met which is basically the  repeal of these three farm laws  those laws are meant to reform the  industry but they now seem to stand in  the way of any progress at all  what's mis